.TH QUADRF-APPLY-AP 8 "August 2026" "QuadRF" "QuadRF"
.SH NAME
quadrf-apply-ap \- set the fallback access point SSID and passphrase
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quadrf-apply-ap
.I ssid
.RI [ passphrase ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Writes
.B QUADRF_AP_SSID
and
.B QUADRF_AP_PASS
into
.IR /etc/quadrf/quadrf.conf ,
regenerates
.IR /etc/hostapd/quadrf.conf
and restarts
.B hostapd
when the fallback access point is already running. An empty
.I passphrase
leaves the AP open
.RB ( wpa=0 ).
A passphrase must be 8–63 characters.
.PP
This does not reboot. Clients associated to the hotspot will be dropped and
have to join the new SSID. If the radio is in client mode, the new settings
are used the next time
.BR quadrf-hotspot (8)
brings the AP up.
.PP
The web control panel invokes this through the sudoers rule in
.IR /etc/sudoers.d/quadrf .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR quadrf (1),
.BR quadrf-hotspot (8),
.BR quadrf-apply-wifi (8),
.BR hostapd.conf (5)
